# Supabase connector MCP — Personal Access Token + default project ref
# (co-located, NOT the product .env). Copy to `mcp/supabase/.env`
# (gitignored) and fill in the real token.
#
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN — Supabase PERSONAL ACCESS TOKEN, sent as
#                         `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Create it at
#                         https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens
#                         ("Account → Access Tokens → Generate new token").
#                         A PAT carries your full account scope across the
#                         Management API (projects, database/query,
#                         migrations) — there is no per-resource scoping on
#                         a PAT, so treat it as a high-privilege SECRET and
#                         never commit the filled .env. (Org/project-scoped
#                         OAuth tokens exist but are out of scope for v1.)
#
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF — the DEFAULT project reference (e.g. abcdefghijklmnop)
#                        used by the project-scoped tools (db.query,
#                        db.list_*, migration.*, project.get) when you do
#                        not pass an explicit project_ref. NOT a secret —
#                        it is the public project reference (the subdomain
#                        of your project's URL: <ref>.supabase.co). Find it
#                        at Project Settings → General → Reference ID, or
#                        via `supabase.project.list`. Optional — leave blank
#                        and pass project_ref per-call if you operate many
#                        projects.
#
# The base URL is fixed (https://api.supabase.com) — no per-tenant host.
# api.supabase.com is NOT behind a Cloudflare WAF, so (unlike the
# cloudflare/hostinger connectors) no browser-style User-Agent is needed.

SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=replace-with-your-supabase-personal-access-token
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=replace-with-your-default-project-ref-or-leave-blank
